IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-homicide.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII: sections 219 to 221 (criminal negligence) and 222 to 228 (homicide).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- A "when" or "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE (the ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c)): marginal reading M2.
-- Answers taken from other sections enter as inputs named for them (`by s 219(1)`, `by s 2 firearm`, `by s 241.1`); the seat layer computes the section 2 answers from facts.

§ `Section 219 -- Criminal negligence`

-- src:4453 | (2) For the purposes of this section, duty means a duty imposed by law.
@ref s 219(2) (src:4453-4453)
GIVEN `it is a duty imposed by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(2) duty` MEANS
    IF `it is a duty imposed by law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "duty means a duty imposed by law"

-- src:4448 | 219 (1) Every one is criminally negligent who
-- src:4449 | (a) in doing anything, or
-- src:4450 | (b) in omitting to do anything that it is his duty to do,
-- src:4451 | shows wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons.
@ref s 219(1) (src:4448-4451)
GIVEN `in doing anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in omitting to do anything that it is his duty to do, by s 219(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person shows wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(1) the person is criminally negligent` MEANS
    IF (`in doing anything` OR `in omitting to do anything that it is his duty to do, by s 219(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person shows wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one is criminally negligent who (a) in doing anything, or (b) in omitting to do anything that it is his duty to do, shows wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons" (marginal reading M1)

§ `Sections 220 and 221 -- Criminal negligence causing death or bodily harm`

-- src:4455 | 220 Every person who by criminal negligence causes death to another person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4456 | (a) where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:4457 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 220 (src:4455-4457)
GIVEN `the person is criminally negligent, by s 219(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by that criminal negligence the person causes death to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220 the person commits the offence of causing death by criminal negligence` MEANS
    IF `the person is criminally negligent, by s 219(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `by that criminal negligence the person causes death to another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who by criminal negligence causes death to another person is guilty of an indictable offence" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 220 (src:4455-4457)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 220 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:4456 | (a) where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
@ref s 220(a) (src:4456-4456)
`s 220(a) four years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE

@ref s 220(a) (src:4456-4456)
`s 220(a) the firearm limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 220(a) four years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4457 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 220(b) (src:4457-4457)
`s 220(b) the other limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4455 | 220 Every person who by criminal negligence causes death to another person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4456 | (a) where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:4457 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 220 (src:4455-4457)
GIVEN `a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 220 the punishment` MEANS
    IF `a firearm is used in the commission of the offence`
    THEN LIST `s 220(a) the firearm limb`
    ELSE LIST `s 220(b) the other limb`

-- src:4459 | 221 Every person who by criminal negligence causes bodily harm to another person is guilty of
-- src:4460 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:4461 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 221 (src:4459-4461)
GIVEN `the person is criminally negligent, by s 219(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by that criminal negligence the person causes bodily harm to another person, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221 the person commits the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` MEANS
    IF `the person is criminally negligent, by s 219(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `by that criminal negligence the person causes bodily harm to another person, by s 2 bodily harm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who by criminal negligence causes bodily harm to another person is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 221 (src:4459-4461)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 221 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 221(a) (src:4460-4460)
`s 221(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 221 (src:4459-4461)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 221 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 221(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 222 -- Homicide`

-- src:4465 | 222 (1) A person commits homicide when, directly or indirectly, by any means, he causes the death of a human being.
@ref s 222(1) (src:4465-4465)
GIVEN `the person causes the death of a human being, directly or indirectly, by any means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(1) the person commits homicide` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the death of a human being, directly or indirectly, by any means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits homicide when, directly or indirectly, by any means, he causes the death of a human being" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4473 | (5) A person commits culpable homicide when he causes the death of a human being,
-- src:4474 | (a) by means of an unlawful act;
-- src:4475 | (b) by criminal negligence;
-- src:4476 | (c) by causing that human being, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do anything that causes his death; or
-- src:4477 | (d) by wilfully frightening that human being, in the case of a child or sick person.
@ref s 222(5) (src:4473-4477)
GIVEN `the person causes the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by criminal negligence, by s 219(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by causing that human being, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do anything that causes his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by wilfully frightening that human being, in the case of a child or sick person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(5) the person commits culpable homicide` MEANS
    IF     `the person causes the death of a human being`
       AND (   `by means of an unlawful act`
            OR `by criminal negligence, by s 219(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `by causing that human being, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do anything that causes his death`
            OR `by wilfully frightening that human being, in the case of a child or sick person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits culpable homicide when he causes the death of a human being, (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4467 | (2) Homicide is culpable or not culpable.
@ref s 222(2) (src:4467-4467)
DECLARE `s 222(2) kind of homicide` IS ONE OF
    `s 222(2) culpable homicide`
    `s 222(2) homicide that is not culpable`

@ref s 222(2) (src:4467-4467)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 222(2) kind of homicide`
`s 222(2) the kind of homicide` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `s 222(2) culpable homicide`
        IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `s 222(2) homicide that is not culpable`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection (5) is itself not covered

-- src:4469 | (3) Homicide that is not culpable is not an offence.
@ref s 222(3) (src:4469-4469)
GIVEN `the person commits homicide, by s 222(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(3) the homicide is an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person commits homicide, by s 222(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Homicide that is not culpable is not an offence"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says only that homicide that is not culpable is not an offence; culpable homicide is made an offence by sections 229 to 240

-- src:4471 | (4) Culpable homicide is murder or manslaughter or infanticide.
@ref s 222(4) (src:4471-4471)
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is murder` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is manslaughter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is infanticide` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(4) culpable homicide is murder or manslaughter or infanticide` MEANS
    IF `it is culpable homicide, by s 222(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`it is murder` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is manslaughter` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is infanticide` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text says culpable homicide is one of the three; a case in which none is answered JUST TRUE is outside what the answers of sections 229, 233 and 234 can say

-- src:4479 | (6) Notwithstanding anything in this section, a person does not commit homicide within the meaning of this Act by reason only that he causes the death of a human being by procuring, by false evidence, the conviction and death of that human being by sentence of the law.
@ref s 222(6) (src:4479-4479)
GIVEN `the person causes the death of a human being by procuring, by false evidence, the conviction and death of that human being by sentence of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only thing by reason of which it is said that he caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(6) the person commits homicide within the meaning of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the death of a human being by procuring, by false evidence, the conviction and death of that human being by sentence of the law` AND `that is the only thing by reason of which it is said that he caused the death`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person does not commit homicide within the meaning of this Act by reason only that he causes the death of a human being by procuring, by false evidence, the conviction and death of that human being by sentence of the law"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that"

§ `Sections 223 to 226 -- Human being; causing death`

-- src:4481 | 223 (1) A child becomes a human being within the meaning of this Act when it has completely proceeded, in a living state, from the body of its mother, whether or not
-- src:4482 | (a) it has breathed;
-- src:4483 | (b) it has an independent circulation; or
-- src:4484 | (c) the navel string is severed.
@ref s 223(1) (src:4481-4484)
-- "whether or not (a) it has breathed; (b) it has an independent circulation; or (c) the navel string is severed": these three facts make no difference, so the function takes none.
GIVEN `it has completely proceeded from the body of its mother` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a living state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(1) the child has become a human being` MEANS
    IF `it has completely proceeded from the body of its mother` AND `it is in a living state`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A child becomes a human being within the meaning of this Act when it has completely proceeded, in a living state, from the body of its mother" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4486 | (2) A person commits homicide when he causes injury to a child before or during its birth as a result of which the child dies after becoming a human being.
@ref s 223(2) (src:4486-4486)
GIVEN `the person causes injury to a child before or during its birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child dies after becoming a human being, as a result of that injury, by s 223(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(2) the person commits homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person causes injury to a child before or during its birth` AND `the child dies after becoming a human being, as a result of that injury, by s 223(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person causes injury to a child before or during its birth` AND `the child dies after becoming a human being, as a result of that injury, by s 223(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection (1) is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits homicide when he causes injury to a child before or during its birth as a result of which the child dies after becoming a human being" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4488 | 224 Where a person, by an act or omission, does any thing that results in the death of a human being, he causes the death of that human being notwithstanding that death from that cause might have been prevented by resorting to proper means.
@ref s 224 (src:4488-4488)
-- "notwithstanding that death from that cause might have been prevented by resorting to proper means": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none.
GIVEN `the person, by an act or omission, does a thing that results in the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 224 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person, by an act or omission, does a thing that results in the death of a human being`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person, by an act or omission, does any thing that results in the death of a human being, he causes the death" (a "where" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4490 | 225 Where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature and from which death results, he causes the death of that human being notwithstanding that the immediate cause of death is proper or improper treatment that is applied in good faith.
@ref s 225 (src:4490-4490)
-- "notwithstanding that the immediate cause of death is proper or improper treatment that is applied in good faith": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none.
GIVEN `the person causes to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `death results from the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 225 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person causes to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature` AND `death results from the injury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature and from which death results, he causes the death" (a "where" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4492 | 226 Where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that results in death, he causes the death of that human being notwithstanding that the effect of the bodily injury is only to accelerate his death from a disease or disorder arising from some other cause.
@ref s 226 (src:4492-4492)
-- "notwithstanding that the effect of the bodily injury is only to accelerate his death from a disease or disorder arising from some other cause": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none.
GIVEN `the person causes to a human being a bodily injury that results in death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person causes to a human being a bodily injury that results in death`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person causes to a human being a bodily injury that results in death, he causes the death" (a "where" condition: marginal reading M2)

§ `Section 227 -- Exemption for medical assistance in dying`

-- src:4502 | (5) In this section, medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner and nurse practitioner have the same meanings as in section 241.1.
@ref s 227(5) (src:4502-4502)
GIVEN `the answer of section 241.1 for the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(5) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` MEANS `the answer of section 241.1 for the term`   -- the same answer as section 241.1 gives for medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner or nurse practitioner

-- src:4498 | (3) For greater certainty, the exemption set out in subsection (1) or (2) applies even if the person invoking it has a reasonable but mistaken belief about any fact that is an element of the exemption.
@ref s 227(3) (src:4498-4498)
GIVEN `the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(3) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` MEANS
    IF `the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the exemption set out in subsection (1) or (2) applies even if the person invoking it has a reasonable but mistaken belief about any fact that is an element of the exemption"

-- src:4494 | 227 (1) No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits culpable homicide if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 227(1) (src:4494-4494)
GIVEN `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 227(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person provides a person with medical assistance in dying, by s 227(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 227(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(1) the practitioner commits culpable homicide` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 227(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the person provides a person with medical assistance in dying, by s 227(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (`it is in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 227(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits culpable homicide if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits culpable homicide if" (the text says nothing of a practitioner who does not provide MAID in accordance with section 241.2)

-- src:4496 | (2) No person is a party to culpable homicide if they do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 227(2) (src:4496-4496)
GIVEN `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 227(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(2) the person is a party to culpable homicide` MEANS
    IF `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying` AND (`it is in accordance with section 241.2` OR `the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief, by s 227(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person is a party to culpable homicide if they do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person is a party to culpable homicide if they do anything for the purpose of aiding"

-- src:4500 | (4) Section 14 does not apply with respect to a person who consents to have death inflicted on them by means of medical assistance in dying provided in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 227(4) (src:4500-4500)
GIVEN `the person consents to have death inflicted on them by means of medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(4) section 14 applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person consents to have death inflicted on them by means of medical assistance in dying` AND `it is provided in accordance with section 241.2`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 14 does not apply with respect to a person who consents to have death inflicted on them by means of medical assistance in dying provided in accordance with section 241.2"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 14 is outside the sources, so whether it applies in any other case is not answered here

§ `Section 228 -- Killing by influence on the mind`

-- src:4504 | 228 No person commits culpable homicide where he causes the death of a human being
-- src:4505 | (a) by any influence on the mind alone, or
-- src:4506 | (b) by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone,
-- src:4507 | but this section does not apply where a person causes the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him.
@ref s 228 (src:4504-4507)
GIVEN `the person causes the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by any influence on the mind alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 the person commits culpable homicide` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the death of a human being` AND (`it is by any influence on the mind alone` OR `it is by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone`) AND (NOT `the person causes the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits culpable homicide where he causes the death of a human being (a) by any influence on the mind alone, or (b) by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone, but this section does not apply where a person causes the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person commits culpable homicide where he causes the death of a human being (a) ... or (b) ..." (the section says nothing of other causes, and does not apply to wilfully frightening a child or sick person)
